                                                "text": "The study of the sounds within stars is known as astroseismology, and a separate report in Science details the findings of more than 500 stars whose deep rumblings Kepler has measured.\nAs convection processes within stars move masses of material up from the core, great pressure waves - in essence, sound waves of very low frequency - are created."
